#X text 721 38 MIDI;
#X text 840 467 Sub-patch borrowed from lecture material;
#X text 527 75 This patch takes an audio signal and pitch shifts it based on the value set by the slider either manually or through MIDI-messages sent to the second inlet. The pitch-shifted signal is delayed and filtered before being sent to the outlet. By sending a MIDI-message to the first inlet \, a feedback loop can be triggered that pitch shifts again for each iteration. The pitchShifter sub-patch is borrowed., f 62;
